OVH: storage cap + auto-prune + DB usage bar in viewer

Prevents the central MySQL database from filling up unbounded.

Backend (PHP):
- config.php: max_snapshots_per_tenant (default 50) and
  max_total_snapshot_mb (default 800, leaving 200MB headroom on 1GB quota).
- ingest.php: after each insert, if total payload exceeds cap, deletes
  oldest snapshots across ALL tenants in batches of 50 until under limit.
  Bounded to max 10 batches per request.
- api.php: two new actions:
    action=usage   - total bytes, percent of cap, per-tenant breakdown
    action=cleanup - manual prune keeping last N per tenant

Frontend:
- UsageBar in viewer: progress bar (green/amber/red at 70/90 percent),
  per-tenant size breakdown, manual Clean button, warning above 90 percent.
- Refreshes every 60s alongside tenant list.
- All 7 locale files updated.
